WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:06.930
It was July, 2007, and the dry New Mexico
heat could shrivel your average outsider into

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.240
the size of a small keychain.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:14.120
Melinda and Bailey, two young women dressed
in impeccable costumes of the Harry Potter

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:19.730
characters Luna Lovegood and Hermione Granger,
were getting ready for a momentous event:

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:25.110
The release of Harry Potter and the Deathly
Hallows, the final installment in the epic

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:30.330
saga of the boy wizard and his quest to defeat
the evil Lord Voldemort.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:36.079
They, like so many other cosplaying fans,
had driven out to Page 1 Books, an exquisite

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:39.030
bookstore in the very heart of Albuquerque.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.960
It was miles from where the two of them lived,
but more than worth the drive to be part of

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:48.519
the Potterhead fever - long before the series’
author would lose her mind on Twitter and

00:00:48.519 --> 00:00:51.890
make the books a lot harder for most people
to enjoy.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:53.380
Trans rights, by the way.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:58.210
Bailey and Melinda were counting the seconds
until the bookstore’s doors finally opened,

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:02.200
and they could get the answers to so many
of their burning questions.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.690
Why had Snape killed Dumbledore?

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:09.590
Would Harry, Ron, and Hermoine find and destroy
the last few Horcruxes, allowing them to finally

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.160
destroy Lord Voldemort once and for all?

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.130
And most importantly of all: Would their ships
sail?

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:22.370
Mel was Harry/Hermoine all the way, but Bailey,
controversially, was all about Ron and Draco.

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:27.040
The two of them couldn’t be more excited
to be part of literary history like this.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:30.450
The bookstore’s doors opened and, little
by little, the line fed in.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:35.640
It was worth the long drive in the late evening
and facing the sweltering summer heat.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.670
When the two of them were holding copies of
Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows, and

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:43.300
walking back to their car, they knew it had
all been worth it.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.650
Mel thought, this must have been how Jesus
felt when he finished writing the first edition

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:49.130
of the Old Testament.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:53.070
History, incidentally, had never been Mel’s
strong suit.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:57.830
Melinda and Bailey set off back to their homes
in the Styx - Bailey was driving; she’d

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:01.610
been kind enough to give Mel a lift, knowing
they were probably their neighborhood’s

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:03.030
biggest Potterheads.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:08.310
It warmed their hearts to see all this enthusiasm
for the book series they loved so fondly,

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:13.129
seeing so many others in costume, or with
vinyl decals or bumper stickers in their cars

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:15.040
declaring their love of the franchise.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.439
They’d seen Hagrid grabbing a Mocha in Starbucks.

00:02:18.439 --> 00:02:21.879
Mad-Eye Moody had been filling up his Buick
at a Gas and Gulp.

00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:26.790
And Sirius Black had passed out from heatstroke
and needed to be attended to medically.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:31.049
With an all-black costume in this kind of
weather, that much was basically inevitable.

00:02:31.049 --> 00:02:35.870
As Bailey and Melinda continued their drive,
drawing closer to the witchy wilderness of

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:40.890
Cibola National Forest, they continued sharing
their thoughts, feelings, and predictions

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.230
about the book to come.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:44.130
They couldn’t wait to read it.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.409
Was it even possible for someone to be this
amped about a book?

00:02:47.409 --> 00:02:53.359
Their enthusiasm was so great, they didn’t
even notice, on those long, winding back roads,

00:02:53.359 --> 00:02:56.319
that another car had started to follow them.

00:02:56.319 --> 00:02:58.130
It was 8:15 PM now.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:59.130
Pitch black.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.930
The kind of darkness where bad things happen.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:07.230
Eventually, during a lull in the conversation,
Mel turned her eyes up to the rear-view mirror

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:09.170
and spotted the car behind them.

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:14.019
It was a car they’d recognize anywhere:
A turquoise-blue Ford Anglia 105E.

00:03:14.019 --> 00:03:20.129
To some, this would be a mostly unrecognizable,
if a little old-fashioned, car, but to Melinda

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:25.870
and Bailey, it could only ever be the enchanted
vehicle of Arthur Weasley - the father of

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:28.250
series mainstay Ron Weasley.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:32.689
The car, which had become iconic since being
featured in the books and films, was able

00:03:32.689 --> 00:03:37.919
to fly and turn invisible, and had gotten
the main characters both into and out of a

00:03:37.919 --> 00:03:40.489
variety of amusing scrapes.

00:03:40.489 --> 00:03:44.889
Mel told Bailey to take a look, and she couldn’t
help but chuckle in admiration.

00:03:44.889 --> 00:03:49.260
Plenty of Harry Potter fans were in town tonight,
and some took it further than others.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:53.779
At times, Bailey wondered if her three Harry
Potter bumper stickers - reading “My Other

00:03:53.779 --> 00:03:58.459
Ride is a Nimbus 2000”, “Save Gas, Take
The Night Bus”, and “All Aboard the Hogwarts

00:03:58.459 --> 00:04:01.609
Express”, respectively - were a little excessive.

00:04:01.609 --> 00:04:06.639
And then there was whoever this was, whose
intense Harry Potter fandom led them to buy

00:04:06.639 --> 00:04:09.189
an authentic Harry Potter car.

00:04:09.189 --> 00:04:12.810
Neither Bailey nor Mel could make out the
driver: The car’s windshield was slightly

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.319
fogged up.

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:17.810
Strange, seeing as it was such a hot evening
out.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:22.190
They noticed that the car also must’ve had
broken turn signals, because any time the

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:26.259
car needed to make a turn, the driver’s
arm would slide out the window and make the

00:04:26.259 --> 00:04:27.780
appropriate gesture.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.120
The Ford Anglia kept pace with them, following
them at every single turn.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:36.840
It was only then that they noticed something
a little odd: The car didn’t have a license

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:37.840
plate.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:42.660
It was almost as though all identifying features
for the car or its driver had been obscured.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:47.759
Bailey, who was getting a little nervous at
this point, decided to try out a little experiment:

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:51.650
At the next three intersections, she took
three left turns.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:55.650
It seemed improbable that anyone would actually
intend to take a route that would lead them

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:59.199
in a circle, and yet, the Ford Anglia did
just that.

00:04:59.199 --> 00:05:04.210
Bailey’s most frightening suspicion was
confirmed: They were being followed.

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:07.860
She didn’t need to tell Melinda, seeing
as the bad vibes radiating off of the car

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:09.379
were already palpable.

00:05:09.379 --> 00:05:12.389
The two assessed their options: They couldn’t
drive home.

00:05:12.389 --> 00:05:16.270
After all, the last thing you want is a crazy
person knowing where you live.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:21.229
Their best bet was to drive to a heavily populated
area - say, the center of Albuquerque during

00:05:21.229 --> 00:05:25.629
one of the most highly-anticipated book launches
in recent memory - or better yet, the local

00:05:25.629 --> 00:05:26.650
police station.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:31.199
Whoever was driving this car wouldn’t dare
try anything there.

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:35.199
Bailey and Melinda sped up and took off in
the direction of the city, but to their horror,

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:37.820
the Ford Anglia sped up in kind.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:41.580
Bailey was pressing the gas pedal down to
the floorboards, and still, the Ford Anglia

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:45.430
gained, its headlights glowing like menacing,
white eyes.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:49.870
In an instant, it pulled ahead of them, the
driver’s hand emerging once again.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:53.039
This time, it signaled for them to stop.

00:05:53.039 --> 00:05:56.729
The two of them would sooner drive their car
off a cliff than stop for whoever was behind

00:05:56.729 --> 00:05:59.270
the murky front window of the Ford Anglia.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:03.900
As the Ford began to slow, perhaps hoping
to box them in, Bailey pounded on the gas

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:07.800
again and lurched forward, weaving around
the Ford and passing it once more.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:12.680
Their two copies of Harry Potter and the Deathly
Hallows were rattling around in the back seats.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:16.710
Neither Bailey nor Melinda expected this night
to end in a car chase.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:21.500
But it wouldn’t be the last time their expectations
would be dashed before sunrise.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.400
The two Potterheads were in the lead again,
but it would still be seven or eight miles

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.710
before they were officially out of Cibola
National Forest.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:32.789
Bailey drove as fast as she could; she and
Melinda were frantic messes of terror and

00:06:32.789 --> 00:06:33.789
adrenaline now.

00:06:33.789 --> 00:06:38.180
But the Ford Anglia kept moving, gaining on
them with every second that passed.

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:40.259
“Go faster, god damn it, faster!”

00:06:40.259 --> 00:06:41.569
Melinda screamed in horror.

00:06:41.569 --> 00:06:43.440
“I’m going as fast as I can!”

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:44.689
Bailey yelped back.

00:06:44.689 --> 00:06:48.080
The car merged into the lane next to them
and sped forwards again.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:51.939
They were neck and neck now, but it was still
too dark inside the other car to make out

00:06:51.939 --> 00:06:53.060
the driver.

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:57.370
Just as Mel was wishing that she could have
a closer look, her wish was granted, in the

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:59.370
worst way possible.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:03.189
The Ford Anglia abruptly moved to the side
and slammed against them, knocking them off

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:05.139
course with the sudden, shocking blow.

00:07:05.139 --> 00:07:10.039
The shock knocked Bailey sideways in the car,
and yanked the steering wheel along with them.

00:07:10.039 --> 00:07:13.889
The car veered off the side of the road and
tumbled down the grassy embankment toward

00:07:13.889 --> 00:07:18.240
the trees, taking the two unfortunate Potterheads
down with it.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:22.300
Before they knew it, their fender was wrapped
around the trunk of a ponderosa pine tree.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:26.500
If it wasn’t for their seatbelts and airbags,
they would have died instantly.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:30.500
But perhaps, in the end, that would have been
a mercy.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:34.240
Melinda and Bailey sat up as the airbags deflated
in front of them.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:35.669
The car was totaled.

00:07:35.669 --> 00:07:39.360
As the two of them shakily unbuckled their
belts and climbed out of the car, they were

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:43.580
bathed in the light of the Ford Anglia’s
headlights from above, as though they were

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:46.620
about to be abducted by a UFO’s tractor
beam.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:51.360
The Ford was just waiting on the road up above
them, its engine rumbling like a low, bestial

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:52.360
growl.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:56.879
The driver was still obscured behind the foggy
windshield, but their arm was hanging out

00:07:56.879 --> 00:07:58.849
of the window once more.

00:07:58.849 --> 00:08:02.550
Bailey and Melinda were too frightened and
dazed by the crash to even move as the car

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:07.289
began advancing, with unnatural grace, down
the embankment before them.

00:08:07.289 --> 00:08:11.639
It clambered towards them with such uncanny
intent that it seemed almost like it had a

00:08:11.639 --> 00:08:16.479
mind of its own, rather than a machine being
piloted by a human being.

00:08:16.479 --> 00:08:19.970
Melinda pointed forwards and screamed; she
saw something Baily didn’t.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:23.130
There was something on the outstretched palm
of the driver’s hand.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:28.719
She thought it was a tattoo at first, until
she saw it move: Two human eyes were fixed

00:08:28.719 --> 00:08:35.050
into the center of the flesh, staring directly
at her - like a crustacean’s eyes on stalks.

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:39.039
Moments later, the car was upon them, and
Melinda’s scream was silenced.

00:08:39.039 --> 00:08:43.820
A concerned passerby found Bailey’s abandoned
car crashed in the ditch beside the road the

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:44.820
next morning.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:49.880
The two women were never found, and two bashed-up
copies of Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:54.870
were discovered on the car’s floor, among
all the shards of broken glass, never to be

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:55.870
read.

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:59.480
Some days can be magical, just not in the
ways you would have hoped.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:06.339
Especially if you run afoul of SCP-3470, a
Euclid-class anomaly somewhat cruelly nicknamed

00:09:06.339 --> 00:09:08.190
“Harry Potter’s Revenge.”

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:12.990
Sadly, kidnappings and car accidents aren’t
that uncommon in this strange, scary world

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:17.840
we live in, but at a certain point, the SCP
Foundation’s many field agents detected

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:23.320
a strange pattern in a series of car accidents
near Cibola National Forest in New Mexico.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:28.480
In all these instances, the cars had been
found crashed, but there were never any bodies.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:32.590
Eagle-eyed police officers studying the crash
sites also picked up another, more subtle

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:38.970
detail in all these events: The cars had turquoise-blue
paint chips on them, even if the cars themselves

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:42.500
weren’t blue, suggesting the impact of another
car.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:46.620
Foundation eggheads correlated this with another
strange report they’d received out of New

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:47.620
Mexico.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:52.410
A young couple had narrowly avoided a dangerous
incident when a car matching the description

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:58.930
of a classic Ford Anglia 105E tried to flag
them down on a dark and lonely road near Cibola

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.510
National Forest.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:05.110
Just like Bailey and Melinda, the duo were
unable to see the driver behind the fogged-up

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:06.110
windshield.

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:09.670
However, when they’d gotten close enough
to see the driver’s hand, they both attested

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:15.209
that it had eyes on its palm - describing
it as similar to the terrifying Pale Man from

00:10:15.209 --> 00:10:17.170
the movie Pan’s Labyrinth.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:21.620
With all of these frightening and clearly
anomalous data points in place, the SCP Foundation

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:26.899
decided it was time to do their due diligence
and go on the hunt for this predatory car.

00:10:26.899 --> 00:10:31.670
It wouldn’t be the first time they’d tackled
a sadistic or carnivorous vehicle, and because

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:34.449
of this experience, they weren’t going in
unprepared.

00:10:34.449 --> 00:10:40.570
There was, of course, SCP-2086, also known
as the Man-Eating Bus.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:45.250
These were a species of huge insect-like creatures,
who’d evolved to perfectly mimic your average

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:49.329
city bus in order to lure prey into their
bodies.

00:10:49.329 --> 00:10:55.010
Another notable instance was SCP-1386, also
known as the Living Ice Cream Van.

00:10:55.010 --> 00:11:00.040
This being is even more mysterious than the
man-eating buses, and boasts a wide range

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:05.630
of abilities, from a hazardous form to a fleshy
appendage somewhat similar to the arm emerging

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:06.630
from SCP-3470.

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:12.139
The jury’s still out on whether either of
these anomalies are in any way directly connected

00:11:12.139 --> 00:11:20.089
to SCP-3470, but it gave the SCP Foundation
a few ideas on how exactly to engage, study,

00:11:20.089 --> 00:11:24.149
and potentially even contain this new vehicular
slaughterer of man.

00:11:24.149 --> 00:11:25.149
Was that last joke kind of a stretch?

00:11:25.149 --> 00:11:26.149
Sorry, they can’t all be winners.

00:11:26.149 --> 00:11:28.760
As you’ve probably come to expect by this
point when there are still so many unknown

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:33.970
variables involved, the Foundation decided
to fall back on old faithful: Throwing a couple

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:36.740
of D-Classes at it and just seeing what happened.

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:42.180
Two were selected, placed in a standard Foundation
off-road vehicle with dash and rear cams,

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:46.550
and given a variety of equipment - Including
a special semi-automatic assault rifle with

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:51.410
armor-piercing rounds, each one containing
a micro-GPS that would allow the Foundation

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:56.040
to continue tracking SCP-3470 after initial
contact.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:12:01.709
And if, in the process of the experiment,
SCP-3470 revealed some frightening new powers,

00:12:01.709 --> 00:12:06.320
then a standard vehicle and a pair of D-Classes
weren’t much of a loss.

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:10.540
Once again, another hapless duo were sent
off on the roads in the proximity of Cibola

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:15.720
National Park, though the Foundation hoped
these two would at least end the night accounted

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:16.720
for.

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:20.440
They patrolled the roads, once or twice remarking
on the beauty of the stars up above, while

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:22.600
not much of anything happened.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:26.810
Command kept close tabs on them back at the
nearest containment site, feeding orders through

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:29.690
earpieces and watching the live video feeds.

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:34.149
As the drive continued, the two D-Classes
finally encountered SCP-3470.

00:12:34.149 --> 00:12:40.959
They get closer, at which point SCP-3470 began
its typical pattern of hunting behavior.

00:12:40.959 --> 00:12:45.959
It merged onto the road next to the D-Class
vehicle and began to sidle alongside them.

00:12:45.959 --> 00:12:49.530
That’s when the two D-Classes realized,
and couldn’t help but remark, that this

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:52.320
looked just like the car from Harry Potter!

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:56.000
Was Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry
a new Group of Interest now?

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:59.630
Had Lord Voldemort entered into allegiance
with the Scarlet King?

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.440
This was hilarious.

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:05.339
Of course, it didn’t remain all that funny
to the D-Classes for long…

00:13:05.339 --> 00:13:08.850
The anomalous Ford Anglia suddenly pulled
up in front of them and ground to an abrupt

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:12.990
halt, forcing the D-Class driving to pound
the brakes, startling both of them.

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:17.070
That’s when the human arm slithered out
from the Anglia’s open window and made the

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:22.700
Stop signal, before twisting around and revealing
the two staring human eyes embedded in its

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:23.720
palm.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:27.470
The D-Classes started to panic and reverse
away while the car started chasing them at

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:29.330
terrifying speeds.

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:33.680
Foundation Command kept ordering the D-Class
riding shotgun to live up to his title and

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:37.930
blast the vehicle with one of the tracking
bullets, but the driver was so terrified,

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:42.010
he refused to slow down and give his fellow
D-Class a clear shot.

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:46.000
As a result, the armed D-Class released a
flurry of shots, and just got lucky that some

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.029
of them happened to strike the car.

00:13:48.029 --> 00:13:52.570
This caused it to let out a terrible, pained
shriek, comparable to the squeal of braking

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:54.020
car tires.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:14:00.360
SCP-3470 then retreated, allowing the D-Classes
to safely return to base while Command tracked

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.860
the Ford Anglia back to its native habitat.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:06.000
It was time for the next phase of the mission
to begin.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:10.250
The Foundation brought in Mobile Task Force
Lambda-12, also known as the Pest Controllers

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:15.130
- a group of operatives who specialize in
taking down particularly verminous creatures.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:21.019
They’d be the ones to track down SCP-3470’s
“nest”, and find out what they were really

00:14:21.019 --> 00:14:22.340
up against here.

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:27.170
In order to complete the mission, four members
of the task force were designated for infiltration,

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:30.430
while two others were designated to keep watch
outside.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:35.230
The infiltrators were given reinforced armor
and a wide selection of weapons and tools,

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:40.280
including a flamethrower, a tranquilizer gun,
a net gun, and a light machine-gun.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:45.240
SCP-3470’s movements were tracked back to
a cave in Cibola National Forest.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:49.390
When the infiltration team entered, they saw
track marks with a familiar tire tread on

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:53.959
the floor and walls of the cave, which suggested
a number of frightening things about the anomaly

00:14:53.959 --> 00:14:55.240
they were chasing.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:59.600
As they got deeper into the cave, the air
became intensely hot and humid.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:04.589
They found scat piles filled with human bones
and a local sheriff’s badge, suggesting

00:15:04.589 --> 00:15:07.850
that the car does indeed eat and digest its
prey.

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:13.470
But most terrifying of all, the infiltration
team discovered a number of translucent eggs,

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:20.089
which had small, quadrupedal organisms - assumed
to be the larval stage of SCP-3470 - wriggling

00:15:20.089 --> 00:15:21.589
away inside.

00:15:21.589 --> 00:15:25.660
They collected some of the eggs and then burned
the rest before turning around to leave.

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:31.190
That’s when they noticed that SCP-3470 was
in the cave mouth, waiting for them.

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:34.170
Except this one wasn’t turquoise, like the
other.

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:36.010
This one was black.

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:38.199
The car began revving aggressively.

00:15:38.199 --> 00:15:42.079
After a tense standoff, in which one of the
task force members muttered, “I refuse to

00:15:42.079 --> 00:15:47.190
be killed by a goddamn Ford”, the task force
member with the light machine gun opened fire

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:49.209
on the car’s exposed arm.

00:15:49.209 --> 00:15:53.190
One of the bullets hit the creature in one
of its hand-eyes, causing it to let out another

00:15:53.190 --> 00:15:58.389
pained shriek and retreat from the cave mouth,
allowing the task force to finally escape.

00:15:58.389 --> 00:16:02.009
The two who were meant to be on look-out were
never seen again.

00:16:02.009 --> 00:16:07.600
SCP-3470 remains at large, with the Pest Controllers
doing whatever they can to track it down and

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:08.600
contain it.

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:10.480
The eggs are also subject to further study.

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:15.240
In the meantime, be careful who you stop for,
because if you end up inside this magical

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:20.269
Ford Anglia, an encounter with the Whomping
Willow is gonna be the least of your worries.

00:16:20.269 --> 00:16:27.800
Now go check out “SCP-1958 - Magic Bus”
and “Living Ice Cream Van SCP-1386” for

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:31.310
more villainous vehicles from the world of
the SCP Foundation!

